remember mythbusters throughout the  2000s and early 2010s mythbusters was  one of the most popular science based  shows in the entire world  every week we got to see their cast put  popular myths and urban legends to the  test is it likely that the alcatraz  prison escape was successful if you  drink that coke and instantly eat mentos  right after would your stomach explode  and most importantly could the jack and  rose have shared the door in titanic  myths like these kept many of us  addicted to the show for several years  but out of nowhere in late 2015 the  mythbusters announced that the longest  running show on the discovery channel  was coming to an end in 2016. for most  of us this was a complete surprise given  that the show was still as entertaining  as ever since then we've seen multiple  spin-offs emerge including mythbusters  the search white rabbit project  mythbusters jr and motor mythbusters  while some of these were great in their  own ride it was of course never as good  as the original  so what happened to mythbusters and why  was the show cancelled  while it may seem like mythbusters ended  abruptly there was actually a slow  fundamental issues that played the team  for years one of these issues was the  chemistry between the team members  themselves specifically adam and jaime  now this might come as a surprise to  many of you but adam and jaime aren't  actually friends and this isn't  speculation or some sort of fan theory  both of them have actually been  extremely transparent about how they  don't actually get along in real life  adam said quote we don't get along very  well together on a personal level in the  25 years that we've known each other  we've never had dinner alone together  similarly when asked if it would be an  exaggeration to say that jamie didn't  really like adam jamie replied  noah we certainly had respect for each  other but we really weren't friends  considering this it's extremely  impressive that this duo was able to  sustain such a productive professional  relationship for so long but if it was  up to them they wouldn't voluntarily  work with each other in other words the  opportunity to work together didn't keep  them on the show by any means they each  had their own independent reasons to do  the show and when those reasons  dissolved it they didn't hesitate to  split ways if you're wondering about the  relationship between tory kerry and  grant these guys were basically the  exact opposite of adam and jaime they  got along extremely well in fact here's  what grant had to say about it the three  of us you tori and i we are beyond  friends we are siblings we shared a  long-a-wild adventure learning from each  other the whole way  our cameraman nicknamed us technical  practical and logical because we were so  different but we could solve any problem  together clearly this trio liked working  with each other but that wasn't enough  to deter them from leaving the show when  the time came either you see interest in  mythbusters was slowly declining over  the years now i know what makes a lot of  you guys upset when i say things like  this because yes even after the decline  mythbusters was still super popular  however when you're constantly trying to  produce bigger seasons with bigger myths  and bigger budgets it's not really  sustainable when viewership and ratings  are declining and according to the data  the decline was pretty clear take a look  at google trends for example the search  data says that interest and myth busters  peaked between 2006 and 2008. there were  two singular peaks in 2009 and 2011 but  for the most part the underlying decline  continued and by the time the show ended  it was only pulling in 20 to 30 percent  of the interest that it was pulling in  during its peak  and if you don't believe google just  listen to adam himself describe the  issue  so mythbusters was on for 14 years  uh every everything in the world has its  own bell curve so we signed that  contract when our ratings were at their  absolute peak and then slowly over the  next five years they started their their  slide they still was respectable ratings  by the end but that slide happened so  while mythbusters were still quite  popular and adored by super fans the  average viewer was starting to tune out  and this makes sense given that the  mythbusters had already tested the most  popular myths there's only so many jack  and rose scenes and water white scenes  that everyone knows  sooner or later you're gonna have to  tackle less popular myths that aren't as  appealing to the general audience and  eventually this led to declining ratings  which took a toll on the show  one of the first shortfalls that was  extremely evident to viewers was what  happened to tory grant and kerry in 2014  it was announced that the b cast would  be eliminated and that the show would  simply focus on adam and jaime according  to the producers what grant carrie and  tori were asking for was unreasonable we  never really got a solid explanation as  to what exactly they asked for or why  negotiations didn't end up fruitful at  first there was some speculation that  this trio might have grown some  resentment for each other just like adam  and jaime but they would soon turn  around and star in the white rabbit  project together so this likely wasn't  the case the more likely scenario is  that the trio wanted to maintain their  compensation or increase it and given  the viewership was declining it this  simply wasn't feasible something else to  note is that it seemed like the trio did  not agree with the direction that the  producers for taking mythbusters  instead of myths being at the center of  each episode it felt like the producers  wanted more explosions and theatrics  they probably thought that this would  help retain viewers but it kind of just  caused the show to lose its original  appeal once carrie grant and tori were  removed from the show ratings just  declined even faster while some viewers  were indifferent to the change most  viewers were upset that they were cut  from the show they felt that the trio  gave a healthy break from the antics of  adam and jaime also carrie was the only  woman that was left on the show  and given that stem fields are generally  skewed towards men many young girls  looked up to carry but unfortunately  this didn't last moving on to the last  two seasons of mythbusters given that  the cast was cut in half the number of  myths tested per show was also cut in  half each episode only covers two mids  instead of three or four like before  on the bright side this allowed the  producers to spend more time showing the  engineering behind each project adam and  jaime also had more time to explain the  science behind each experiment while  these facets were welcomed by superfans  to the average viewer this likely just  felt slower paced and not as exciting  and soon enough adam and jaime's  five-year contract was coming to an end  as well meaning that it was time to  renegotiate adam was actually super  transparent about this stating that he  simply wasn't willing to do the show for  less compensation  do you keep the show going well  discovery's not going to want to pay us  more to keep on doing the show and  frankly after 14 years and i'm 50 now  i'm tired i'm definitely not going gonna  do the show for less and given that  discovery wasn't willing to allocate a  bigger budget the only option was to  shut it down the silver lining is the  discovery that jamie and adam and the  show on their terms they were allowed to  call it a final season and they were  able to test some of the biggest myths  yet but the best part was that they were  able to invite kyrie torre and grant to  do a wrap up episode this conclusion was  extremely well received by the fans  given that it was the highest rated  mythbusters episode of all time so while  it was a shame that mythbusters came to  an end earlier than people wanted it's  nice that the show at least got the  ending that it deserved  in terms of what the mythbusters are up  to today they've all gone down their own  paths starting with adam while he left  mythbusters he never really gave up the  show business he went on to host two  more shows called the mythbusters junior  and savage builds  given the name mythbusters jr i don't  think you'd be surprised here that he  had a similar premise to the original  show instead of how adults test these  mitts however he had teenagers and adam  was basically their mentor leading them  through the design assembly and testing  processes as for savage builds this show  was focused on new inventions and  restoration projects adam collaborated  with industry experts and friends to  make things like the iron man suit and  the wheel of death savage builds  actually performed quite well however  both of these shows were canceled after  just one season adam wasn't just  involved in tv shows either he also had  a cameo in 2048 didn't know where to run  it and he published a book called every  tool as a hammer life is what you make  it likely his most significant project  over the past several years however is  his youtube channel adam became the face  of the youtube channel tested and they  even renamed the channel to adam  savage's tested the channel has nearly 6  million subscribers and they post a new  video almost every day about science and  the building anyway moving on to jaime  his life after mythbusters hasn't been  nearly as eventful he has more or less  left the show business and has mainly  focused on personal projects for example  he built a tank that's specifically  designed for firefighting he also  received an honorary doctorate in  technology from la penrantan university  of technology in 2017. this was actually  his third honorary doctorate he had  previously received one from villanova  university and the university of tuente  more recently he was appointed as a  professor at luck university in november  of 2021 this was a five-year contract so  this is probably where i'll spend the  majority of his time in the coming years  moving on to tori he's basically just  jumped from one show to another shortly  after mythbusters ended he started  hosting a show called the thrill factor  with kerry the show focuses on the  science and engineering behind roller  coasters and amusement park rides and  explains why certain attractions are so  thrilling after throw factor torrey went  on to host white rabbit project with of  course carrion grant he took a few years  off from the show business after white  rabbit project but he eventually  returned in 2019 with the great  escapists since then he's also appeared  on the explosion show and the jackass  forever so things haven't changed all  that much for tori the same can be said  about kerry as well she of course also  hosted welfare and white rabbit project  but she's done a few things on her own  as well for example she hosted crash  test world this show focuses on the tech  capitals of the world and how these  various cities are helping build our  future aside from starring in these  shows carrie also helped found an  educational streaming service called  explore media the streaming service is  still super new so we'll have to see how  it plays out and finally last but  definitely not least we have grant after  mythbusters and white rabbit project  rand went on to host the second season  of home of the future as the name  suggests this show focuses on futuristic  homes filled with the newest tech grant  also had a cameo in the tv movie  sharknado 3. grant hasn't just been  working on the front end of movies and  tv shows either he also spent a lot of  time on the back end as well for example  in 2017 he consulted with the disney for  six months to help them build better  animatronics while things were going  pretty good for granted career-wise he  would unfortunately be hit with an  intracranial aneurysm in july of 2020  which took his life he was only 49 years  old at the time which leaves him with  the most tragic ending  while it's already been several years  since mythbusters ended i'd be blank to  bet that the effect of mythbusters will  live on for decades mythbusters inspired  millions of kids and teenagers to pursue  careers in science and engineering and  who knows what these young minds will  come up with in the coming decades in  terms of the show itself ending it it  really just came down to declining  viewership and a limited budget but  honestly i don't think it's necessarily  a bad thing more times than not we see  shows go on for way too long  mythbusters was able to end off at a  time where viewers still wanted more  which is why all of us still remember it  in such a positive light even after all  these years  and i'm not sure if any other ending  could have created such a lasting effect  but that's just what i think did you  watch mythbusters growing up comment  that down below also drop a like if  you're glad that mythbusters ended up  strong and of course consider joining  our discord community suggested ideas  and consider subscribing to more  questions possibly answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  you

